<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 12+ (API 31) SYSTEM splash override.

  On API 31+ the platform draws its OWN splash and reads ONLY android:-prefixed
  attributes here (the androidx non-prefixed ones in values/styles.xml don't apply
  on 31+). By default the OS masks the LAUNCHER adaptive-icon into a circle on every
  cold start — that was the original "navy bg with a circle of the stale wordmark"
  that flashed when the evicted process is re-opened.

  We now show an INTENTIONAL brand splash: @drawable/splash_icon is the colorful
  LEXI CLASH brand art (same master as the launcher icon, resources/icon-only.png),
  recolored to a navy bg and pre-padded to ~62% so it sits inside the circle safe-zone
  and never gets clipped. windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor + background are both neo-navy
  (#1a1a2e) — matching the launch + post-splash window backgrounds — so the mark reads
  as a clean brand badge on seamless navy, and the navy→app handoff stays invisible.
  This is the splash users expect, NOT the broken clipped flash.

  NOTE (honest caveat): a few OEM skins (e.g. older Samsung One UI) render the system
  splash icon at slightly different scale/margins — the safe-zone padding makes that a
  cosmetic difference, not a clipped logo.

  ⚠️ DO NOT run `npx capacitor-assets generate` — it can rewrite these themes back to
  the full-wordmark @drawable/splash and reintroduce the flash.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">#FF1A1A2E</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor">#FF1A1A2E</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/AppTheme.NoActionBar</item>
    </style>
</resources>
